    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "This matter is taken up through Hybrid Arrangement  (Virtual/Physical Mode).\n2. Since the criminal revision pertains to prayer for release of the petitioner on bail in connection with offence under Section 376(3) of IPC and Section 6 of POCSO Act, the informant and victim are required to be noticed and informed before any order passed in revision in view of the provision under Section 439(1A) of CrPC and Sub-rule 13 and 15 (viii) of Rule-4 of the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Rules, 2020 (in short the \"Rules\").\n3. For the purpose of notice to the informant and information of victim-child in terms of the above Act and Rules, let the copy of the revision petition received by the learned counsel for the State be sent to the informant and victim by Mr. R.B.Mishra, learned Addl. Public Prosecutor through concerned Police Station indicating therein the probable date of hearing.\n4. Further, the petitioner is directed to apprise the Court about passing of any preliminary assessment order in this case and at the same time, the State counsel is requested to produce Social Investigation Report (SIR) of the child and Social Background Report of the child from Child Welfare Police Officer by next date.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
